layout "layout.faqir"

block content
  p
    | Every computer where you use Claude Code needs to be
    strong paired
    | once before Buildyboy can see its sessions. Pairing gives the computer its own access key and installs the Buildyboy
    | plugin into Claude Code. This page covers pairing on each system, checking that it worked, and managing machines
    | afterwards.

  h2#pair Pairing a machine
  ol
    li
      | Open
      strong Machines
      | and press
      strong Pair a machine
      | .
    li
      | Type a name in
      strong Name for this machine (optional)
      | , for example
      code work-laptop
      | , and press
      strong Create pairing code
      | . (Without a name, the computer's own host name is used.)
    li
      | An 8-character code appears with a countdown (
      code Expires in 09:58
      | ). It works once and expires after 10 minutes; if it runs out, press
      strong New code
      | .
    li Copy the command for the computer's system and run it there, in a normal terminal (not inside Claude Code).
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="machines-pair-desktop.png" alt="The Pair a machine panel with a pairing code, its expiry countdown and the two install commands." caption="The pairing panel. The commands already contain the code and this server's address.")

  h3#pair-linux Linux, macOS and WSL
  pre
    code
      | curl -fsSL {{ site.url }}/install.sh | bash -s -- PAIRCODE
  p
    | Needs
    code curl
    | ,
    code tar
    | and Node.js (Claude Code's hooks are Node scripts). Add
    code --name laptop-wsl
    | after the code to choose the name here instead.
  h3#pair-windows Windows (PowerShell)
  pre
    code
      | $env:BB_CODE='PAIRCODE'; irm {{ site.url }}/install.ps1 | iex
  p
    | Run it in Windows PowerShell or PowerShell 7 (not in Command Prompt). It needs Windows 10 version 1803 or newer. Set
    code $env:BB_NAME='laptop'
    | first to choose the name.
  +callout(variant="warning")
    @content
      p
        | The code stays in
        code $env:BB_CODE
        | for as long as that PowerShell window is open. If you need to pair again, create a new code and set it again,
        | or open a new window; re-running the line as it is reuses the spent code and fails.

  h3#what-it-does What the installer does
  ol
    li
      | Downloads the plugin into
      code ~/.buildyboy/marketplace
      | .
    li
      | Pairs the machine and saves its address, key and id in
      code ~/.buildyboy/config.json
      | , readable only by you.
    li
      | Registers the plugin with Claude Code (
      code claude plugin marketplace add
      | and
      code claude plugin install buildyboy@buildyboy
      | ).
    li
      | Optionally installs the
      a(href="/docs/runner") runner
      | .
    li Sends a test event, so the machine shows up straight away.
  p
    | It finishes with "Buildyboy is installed on …". It never edits your Claude Code settings file
    code ~/.claude/settings.json
    | .

  h2#windows-and-wsl Windows and WSL
  p
    | Windows and WSL keep separate Claude Code folders, so for Buildyboy they are two machines. If you use Claude Code in
    | both, pair both, each with its own code, and give them different names (for example
    code laptop
    | and
    code laptop-wsl
    | ): they usually share the same host name, so without a name you get two machines called the same.

  h2#check Checking a machine
  ol
    li Start a new Claude Code session on it. Sessions that were already open do not have the plugin yet.
    li
      | Type
      code /bb-status
      | . A healthy machine answers like this:
  pre
    code
      | Server: {{ site.url }} (reachable)
      | Machine: work-laptop (m_8c1f…)
      | Walk mode: off for this session
      | Spool: 0 bytes waiting locally
      | Session: {{ site.url }}/s/1b2c…
  p
    | If it says the server is
    strong NOT reachable
    | , the machine cannot reach your server (check the address and your network). The session keeps working normally;
    | events wait in the spool.
  p
    | The session should now be on the
    a(href="/docs/floor") Floor
    | . After installing you may also see a short session named "install-test-…"; that is the installer's test event and
    | can be ignored.

  h2#machines-page The Machines page
  p Each machine has a card:
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="machines-desktop.png" alt="Machine cards with a status badge, platform, Claude Code and hook versions, last event, spool size, runner state and a three-way walk mode control." caption="Machine cards.")
  dl
    dt Status badge
    dd
      code online
      | (it sent something in the last 5 minutes, or its runner is connected),
      code offline
      | , or
      code revoked
      | .
    dt Platform, Claude Code, Hook
    dd The system and host name, the Claude Code version and the plugin version.
    dt Last event
    dd When it last sent something. Amber after 10 quiet minutes.
    dt Spool
    dd How much is waiting on that machine to be sent. Normally 0 B.
    dt Runner
    dd
      code connected
      | or
      code not running
      | .
    dt Walk mode
    dd
      strong Inherit
      | (follows the global setting),
      strong On
      | (always on for this machine) or
      strong Off
      | (never waits for you here). See
      a(href="/docs/walk-mode#which-wins") Walk mode
      | .
  h3#rename Renaming
  p
    | Press
    strong Rename
    | , type the new name and press
    strong Save
    | .
  h3#rotate Giving a machine a new key
  p
    | If you think a machine's key has leaked, press
    strong Rotate token
    | and then
    strong Rotate now
    | . The old key stops working immediately. The new one is shown
    strong once
    | (copy it with
    strong Copy token
    | ): put it in the
    code token
    | field of
    code ~/.buildyboy/config.json
    | on that machine, or simply pair the machine again with a new code.
  h3#revoke Removing a machine
  ol
    li
      | On the machine, run the installer with the uninstall switch. It removes the plugin and the runner and asks before
      | deleting
      code ~/.buildyboy
      | :
  pre
    code
      | curl -fsSL {{ site.url }}/install.sh | bash -s -- --uninstall
  pre
    code
      | $env:BB_UNINSTALL='1'; irm {{ site.url }}/install.ps1 | iex
  ol(start="2")
    li
      | In Buildyboy, press
      strong Revoke
      | on the machine's card and confirm with
      strong Revoke <name>
      | . Its hooks and runner are cut off for good; its history stays. To use it again, pair it again.
  p Revoked machines stay in the list, dimmed, so their history keeps its context.

  h2#by-hand Pairing without the installer
  p
    | If you cannot pipe a script into your shell, pair with Buildyboy's command-line tool from a copy of the code, then
    | register the plugin yourself:
  pre
    code
      | node cli/bb.ts pair {{ site.url }} PAIRCODE my-laptop
      | claude plugin marketplace add ~/.buildyboy/marketplace
      | claude plugin install buildyboy@buildyboy
  p
    | The first command writes
    code ~/.buildyboy/config.json
    | ; the marketplace folder comes from the installer or from
    code {{ site.url }}/plugin.tgz
    | .
